---
// SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
// SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 The WeaveSignal contributors
// The status strip under the hero (ADR-0211): the release, and what is proven, early and not yet,
// from "What release one does, and what it leaves out" and the changelog's known limits. Keep it
// current at each release.
import Agpl from './Agpl.astro';
---

<section class="status" aria-labelledby="status-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="version">
      <strong id="status-h">1.0.1</strong>
      <span>12 November 2026</span>
      <span class="more"><a href="/docs/reference/release-one-status/">The full status</a></span>
    </div>
    <dl>
      <div>
        <dt>Proven</dt>
        <dd>A real caller rang a public station from a phone and went to air. A station streamed for 24 hours on a server of its own with no restart. A guest's return arrives 69–77 ms after the voice on one machine.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Early</dt>
        <dd>Two people talking over two real networks is measured, not yet judged by ear. Video has gone from a guest's browser camera through a station on Cloudron to an RTMP server, not yet through a whole show. The Windows installer is built, unsigned, and has not been run on Windows.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Not yet</dt>
        <dd>Callers from a telephone number. WHIP for remote DJs and the presenter kit. A macOS build. The Cloudron app store listing.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <Agpl />
  </div>
</section>
